Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:51:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] perf: render video wallpapers at the video's frame rate

The render loop runs at --fps (30 by default) even when the only thing on
screen is a 24 fps video, so every fifth frame redraws the same video frame.

GLPlayer now reads mpv's container-fps when the video is configured, CVideo
reports it through a new CWallpaper::getContentFrameRate () (0 = can change on
any frame), and the main loop lowers the target rate to the fastest video when
every output shows a plain video. --fps stays the upper bound, and scenes, web
wallpapers and videos inside scenes keep the full rate. The Wayland and GLFW
drivers now read the target rate every frame instead of caching --fps.

1080p24 video wallpaper on niri: 23.4 rendered frames/s instead of 29.0 (with the
previous fix only); scene wallpapers unchanged at ~29.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
